Portions of this directory are adapted from claude-mathematician by
Konstantin Gerbig: the rule that a verdict exists only if an executed script
printed it, the verdict names VERIFIED, VERIFIED-NUMERICALLY, FAILED and
UNCHECKED, the one-script-per-check layout, and the shape of the runner that
writes RESULTS.md.

Sanity replaces those names with HOLDS, FAILS and UNCHECKED plus an evidence
kind (proof, symbolic, asymptotic, numerical, refutation, counterexample), adds
Lean and verdicts.json, and does not use Mathematica. The adapted files are check_template.py and
verify_run.py. This directory is the Verifier (formerly the Checker).

